[["Map",1,2,29,30],"lessons",["Map",3,4],"imperatives",{"id":3,"data":5,"body":25,"filePath":26,"digest":27,"deferredRender":28},{"lessonId":6,"title":7,"description":8,"level":9,"kind":10,"slug":3,"order":11,"status":12,"durationMinutes":13,"objectives":14,"skills":18,"prerequisites":21,"audioClips":23,"updated":24},"a1-imperatives","Instructions with the imperative","Learn how English uses the base verb for clear directions, instructions, warnings, invitations, and appropriately softened requests.","A1","grammar",10,"published",60,[15,16,17],"Give clear positive and negative instructions.","Adjust direct instructions for an appropriate social tone.","Sequence a short real-world procedure.",[10,19,20],"speaking","functional-language",[22],"a1-object-pronouns",[],["Date","2026-07-12T00:00:00.000Z"],"import LessonFlow from '../../../components/LessonFlow.astro';\nimport PromptCard from '../../../components/PromptCard.astro';\nimport Quiz from '../../../components/Quiz.astro';\nimport ThinkingCard from '../../../components/ThinkingCard.astro';\n\n\u003CLessonFlow steps={[\n  { label: 'Notice', description: 'Follow useful instructions.' },\n  { label: 'Discover', description: 'See why the listener is understood.' },\n  { label: 'Build', description: 'Sequence and soften instructions.' },\n  { label: 'Use', description: 'Guide another person clearly.' },\n]} />\n\n## Notice before the rule\n\n\u003CThinkingCard title=\"First-day instructions\">\n  \u003Cp>\u003Cem>Come in. Please take a seat. Write your name here. Don’t sign the second page. Ask me if you need help.\u003C/em>\u003C/p>\n  \u003Cul>\n    \u003Cli>What form begins each instruction?\u003C/li>\n    \u003Cli>Is the subject \u003Cem>you\u003C/em> written?\u003C/li>\n    \u003Cli>How does the negative instruction begin?\u003C/li>\n  \u003C/ul>\n\u003C/ThinkingCard>\n\n## Get to the root: the listener is understood\n\nAn imperative begins with the base verb because the subject **you** is normally understood from the situation. The speaker directs the words toward the listener: *(You) open the file.* English leaves *you* unspoken because it is already obvious.\n\nThe grammar is compact, but the social meaning depends on context. *Turn left* can be helpful directions. *Take one tablet with food* can be medical instructions. *Don’t move* can be an urgent warning.\n\n| Purpose | Pattern | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Positive instruction | base verb | Save the document. |\n| Negative instruction | don’t + base verb | Don’t delete the original. |\n| Polite direct request | please + imperative | Please send me the address. |\n| Shared suggestion | let’s + base verb | Let’s check it together. |\n\n## Tone changes the relationship\n\nA bare imperative can be neutral, friendly, urgent, or rude. Instructions on a screen are neutral. The same form spoken to a coworker may need *please* or a request with *Can you…?*\n\n| Form | Typical effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| Send me the address. | clear and direct |\n| Please send me the address. | polite, but still direct |\n| Can you send me the address? | framed as a request |\n| Let’s check the address. | includes speaker and listener |\n\n## Use it in real life\n\n\u003CPromptCard label=\"Give directions\">Guide the teacher from your home to a useful place nearby.\u003C/PromptCard>\n\u003CPromptCard label=\"Explain a process\">Explain how to join a video call or make your favorite hot drink.\u003C/PromptCard>\n\u003CPromptCard label=\"Friendly host\">Welcome a visitor using five appropriate instructions, offers, or invitations.\u003C/PromptCard>\n\n## Reflect\n\nExplain why the subject is normally absent in an imperative. Then give one positive instruction, one negative warning, and one softened request.\n\n\u003CQuiz\n  title=\"Final check: form, meaning, and tone\"\n  successMessage=\"Excellent. You can give clear instructions and adjust their social tone.\"\n  items={[\n    { question: '___ the document.', answer: 'Open', options: ['Open', 'You open', 'To open'] },\n    { question: '___ here.', answer: \"Don’t park\", options: [\"Don’t park\", 'Not park', \"Don’t parking\"] },\n    { question: 'Which option includes both people?', answer: 'Let’s start.', options: ['Start.', 'Let’s start.', 'You start.'] },\n  ]}\n/>","src/content/lessons/a1/imperatives.mdx","e82abf4b1a015616",true,"meta::meta",["Map",31,32,33,34,35,36],"astro-config-digest","{\"root\":{},\"srcDir\":{},\"publicDir\":{},\"outDir\":{},\"cacheDir\":{},\"site\":\"http://localhost:4321\",\"compressHTML\":\"jsx\",\"base\":\"/\",\"trailingSlash\":\"ignore\",\"output\":\"static\",\"scopedStyleStrategy\":\"attribute\",\"build\":{\"format\":\"directory\",\"client\":{},\"server\":{},\"assets\":\"_astro\",\"serverEntry\":\"entry.mjs\",\"redirects\":true,\"inlineStylesheets\":\"auto\",\"concurrency\":1},\"server\":{\"open\":false,\"host\":false,\"port\":4321,\"allowedHosts\":[]},\"redirects\":{\"/English Curriculum Map.html\":\"/curriculum/\",\"/lessons/a0/animals.html\":\"/lessons/a0/animals/\",\"/lessons/a0/articles-a-an.html\":\"/lessons/a0/articles-a-an/\",\"/lessons/a0/cardinal-numbers-0-100.html\":\"/lessons/a0/cardinal-numbers-0-100/\",\"/lessons/a0/classroom-objects.html\":\"/lessons/a0/classroom-objects/\",\"/lessons/a0/colours-and-basic-adjectives.html\":\"/lessons/a0/colours-and-basic-adjectives/\",\"/lessons/a0/countries-and-nationalities.html\":\"/lessons/a0/countries-and-nationalities/\",\"/lessons/a0/days-months-dates.html\":\"/lessons/a0/days-months-dates/\",\"/lessons/a0/family-members.html\":\"/lessons/a0/family-members/\",\"/lessons/a0/greetings-and-introductions.html\":\"/lessons/a0/greetings-and-introductions/\",\"/lessons/a0/possessive-adjectives.html\":\"/lessons/a0/possessive-adjectives/\",\"/lessons/a0/question-words-what-where-who-how.html\":\"/lessons/a0/question-words-what-where-who-how/\",\"/lessons/a0/regular-plural-nouns.html\":\"/lessons/a0/regular-plural-nouns/\",\"/lessons/a0/subject-pronouns.html\":\"/lesson